cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GUI to ADCP Docking"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it and the docking engine it runs.
  ADCP (AutoDock CrankPep) and ADFRsuite were developed by the Scripps
  Research Institute and are not part of this work; this package is a
  browser and command-line workflow that runs them. The full citation list
  for a run, including the preparation and rescoring tools it used, is
  printed by `adcp-dock cite <run>`.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aadhil
    family-names: Haq
    affiliation: "HOPE Lab, Texas A&M University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8335-2121"
  - given-names: Sandun
    family-names: Fernando
    affiliation: "HOPE Lab, Texas A&M University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7692-2170"
version: "0.1.14"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
abstract: >-
  Browser and command-line workflow for peptide docking with AutoDock
  CrankPep (ADCP 1.0 and 1.1). It connects receptor preparation, grid
  generation, docking, optional MM-GBSA rescoring or ADCP 1.1's OpenMM
  minimization, and reporting, and runs on a Slurm cluster, a local computer
  or Google Colab. With ADCP 1.1 it accepts non-standard and D amino acids,
  and a run can start from a target file made in AGFRGUI.
keywords:
  - peptide docking
  - ADCP
  - molecular docking
  - MM-GBSA
  - OpenMM
  - non-standard amino acids
  - high-performance computing
